# TUI viewport & acceptance discipline

Derived from [docs/LESSONS-LEARNED-VIEWPORT-HARDENING.md](../../docs/LESSONS-LEARNED-VIEWPORT-HARDENING.md).

## Never weaken the contract

- Do **not** skip, xfail, or rewrite viewport/collapse/Tools-action tests to accommodate broken layout or click behavior.
- Keyboard bindings (F3/F4) are parallel affordances, not replacements for mouse restore on `#nav-collapse` / `#right-collapse`.
- Do **not** call `scroll_to_widget(#update)` (or similar) only inside a test to hide off-screen actions.

## Collapse / restore controls

- One physical click → exactly one state transition (`left_nav_collapsed` / `right_panel_collapsed`, CSS `collapsed`, button label, nav-button display must agree).
- Toggle buttons must remain clickable after collapse. Enlarge the rail if needed; there is no product requirement that a collapsed rail be exactly five columns.
- Textual `Button` ignores clicks while class `-active` is set. For toggle rails set `active_effect_duration = 0` (and prefer `compact=True`) so a fast restore click still calls `press()`.

```python
# ✅ toggle control
button = Button("<", id="nav-collapse", compact=True)
button.active_effect_duration = 0
```

## Surface navigation

- `#surface` and the route’s `#actions` belong on one operational block (e.g. `#operation`).
- `show_surface(route)` must scroll that operational block into view so Tools actions (Verify, Check Updates, Update, Open CodeSleuth) are clickable at `120x35` without test-specific scrolling.
- Branding/status must not push the navigated-to actions below the fold.

## Docs controller contract

- Canonical section: README `### OpenCode \`build\` controller` → `#opencode-build-controller`.
- Product/branding/maintainer docs link with `../README.md#opencode-build-controller`.
- Do not copy the controller diagram (`native provider-specific controller prompt`) into those docs.

## Acceptance before claiming done

- Run the focused viewport/docs tests, then full `pytest`, `ruff check .`, and Bun smokes.
- Manually exercise collapse↔restore and Tools actions at least at `80x24`, `120x35`, `140x40`.
- If Pilot says the click hit the widget but state did not change, check `-active` / Pressed handlers before blaming geometry.
